ether  clues and survive and you'll not believe  how Keira fiying some simple pixel art  can be but nothing screams indie game  more than Octodad dadliest catch from  young heroes it's available for PC and  ps4 in the game you control the  eponymous Octodad who is an octopus  desperately trying to hide the fact that  he isn't human from his family you  control octodad's boneless tentacle arms  with the analog sticks but it isn't easy  and you'll find yourself being as clumsy  inept and silly as you might expect an  oxygen breathing octopus wearing a suit  to be on land this game exemplifies the  indie spirit so there you have it five  great indie titles sure to spark the  imagination challenge the reflexes and  question the status quo in mainstream  gaming if you've got a gamer on your  list who loves the indie scene or even  just one excited to try something  different you can't go wrong with any of  these picks  i'm jeff kannada thanks for watching
 

